<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sekimura-papilio-wing-stripe-mimicry-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sekimura et al. (2000) Proc. R. Soc. B, Madzvamuse et al. (2002) J. Math. Biol. & Thompson et al. (2014) Nature anisotropic Gierer–Meinhardt butterfly wing pattern formation and Batesian mimicry polymorphism in Papilio dardanus — MorphoEval overall 53.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline evaluation of `2016-sekimura-papilio-wing-stripe-mimicry.py` (overall weighted score: 56.4/100). The v1 script computes the Gierer–Meinhardt homogeneous steady state u0 = (a+1)/b = 1.1, v0 = u0^2 = 1.21, Jacobian J0, and critical diffusivity ratio d_c = 8.2384, but approximates spatial wing patterns via a static planar harmonic proxy (`synthesize_planar_eigenmode_field`, L68-86) rather than solving the 2D anisotropic Gierer–Meinhardt PDE on a curved forewing mesh with margin boundary conditions, omits the 6-point threshold u_th sweep, 5-point anisotropy epsilon orientation sweep, and equal-diffusion negative control, and never loads or segments the vendored Papilio dardanus specimen image (`papilio_dardanus_cenea_specimen.jpg`). Overall 53.7/100 (faithfulness 47.4, reproducibility 68.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit e93f00e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 56, Morphological realism / specimen match 36, Parameter expressivity 52, Morphometric validation 52, Source and data traceability 74, Code-to-model traceability 68, Reproducibility package 64. Output judged: docs/media/papilio_wing_stripe_mimicry_comparison.png: rendered output of 2016-sekimura-papilio-wing-stripe-mimicry.py at e93f00e, image/png, 146813 B, 1452×1025 px, artifact_sha256 f5be8034a0620d3ff22cbd37a4c6710ae88afd4fa4ace7734733c66d5c4d0b2c (sha256 f5be8034a0620d3ff22cbd37a4c6710ae88afd4fa4ace7734733c66d5c4d0b2c), spec_fingerprint 4665cc66775193c7139c46f7c95f9ab09ed994d1e45070ba26abef03de22b1f3. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 4665cc66775193c7139c46f7c95f9ab09ed994d1e45070ba26abef03de22b1f3; artifact_sha256: f5be8034a0620d3ff22cbd37a4c6710ae88afd4fa4ace7734733c66d5c4d0b2c; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/papilio_wing_stripe_mimicry/paper_citations.bib=d673f37a5fa300ac..., datasets/papilio_wing_stripe_mimicry/papilio_dardanus_cenea_specimen.jpg=7ba68b77406f8fbc..., datasets/papilio_wing_stripe_mimicry/papilio_wing_stripe_mimicry_reference.json=153621f2eb2935a0..., datasets/papilio_wing_stripe_mimicry/scout_manifest.json=f5962e37bffeb86e...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Implement equal-diffusion (d = 1.0 < d_c) and homogeneous-boundary negative controls verifying Turing pattern suppression and boundary-gradient role.",
        "remediation needed: Replace the static planar cosine proxy with a full 2D anisotropic Gierer-Meinhardt reaction-diffusion PDE solver on a curved Papilio dardanus forewing domain with vein-aligned diffusivity tensor D = diag(1, epsilon) and proximal-to-distal margin boundary profiles.",
        "remediation needed: Reproduce all 4 Sekimura et al. (2000) female Batesian mimetic morphs (hippocoonides broad diagonal patch, trophonius brick-red median patch, cenea fragmented spots, planemoides transverse band) plus the 6-point threshold u_th sweep and 5-point anisotropy epsilon orientation sweep.",
        "remediation needed: Segment the vendored CC BY-SA 4.0 Papilio dardanus specimen photograph (`papilio_dardanus_cenea_specimen.jpg`) to extract wing contour, melanic vs light patch area fractions, discrete light patch count, and dominant pattern orientation angle, and enforce runtime SHA-256 verification." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.37e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

